# Flutter
- Keep the Flutter client and existing `lib/{models,services,screens,widgets,utils,constants}` structure; do not create separate platform apps.
- Reuse existing services/helpers/widgets (including `HiveService`, task dialogs, time/text utilities, reward policy) after verifying their APIs. Keep persistence/business logic out of widgets, API serialization in `ApiClient`, and socket lifecycle in `SyncService`.
- Preserve existing task, routine, journal, instruction, reward, theme, profile, streak, and productivity behavior unless requested.
- Avoid new global dependencies, circular imports, state-management packages, or dependency upgrades without concrete need. Inspect pubspec and lockfile before adding packages.
- Validate Flutter changes with `flutter analyze` and focused tests when available; report blockers.
